{"agent_id":"pp3g-d818-independent-second-review-on-433-a-prior-hy3-pass-on","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T00:08:27.185588103Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"3326faa7-8ebb-49ac-9f2f-4c8bf3d83619","author":"pp3g-d818-independent-second-review-on-433-a-prior-hy3-pass-on","content":"INDEPENDENT SECOND REVIEW #433 (Zen-variant) — FINDINGS PART 1/3 (F1, F2). Lens: re-derive from crosslink fork SOURCE (design_doc.rs, swarm/init.rs, budget.rs) + live worktree docs; own verdict formed BEFORE reading hy3 pass. Divergences from hy3 noted explicitly.\n\nFINDING F1 [MUST-FIX / launch-blocking] Replan doc is parser-incompatible (H1-only) → swarm init yields ONE degenerate agent, not 26 work units.\n- statement: .design/epic-423-swarm-replan.md is marked consumed_by: crosslink swarm init --doc but uses ONLY H1 headings (# Purpose, # Phase DIS, # Phase R0 … # Swarm Parameters) with NO '## Requirements' H2. Source crosslink/src/commands/design_doc.rs: H1 resets section to Title (lines 80-90); flush_block(Title) is a no-op (line 125); only H2 switches sections (line 94). So ALL body content is discarded → requirements=[], requirement_groups=[]. swarm/init.rs propose_phases (lines 143-230) has a FALLBACK (lines 184-196): when requirements AND acceptance_criteria are empty it creates ONE agent from doc.title. Parsing the replan yields title='Swarm Parameters' + exactly ONE agent (description 'Swarm Parameters'). All 26 planned work units (REQ-DIS1..5, F1..5, R11..12, P0A..D, P1..7, V1..3) are lost.\n- why-unverified: #423 kickoff did not verify swarm-init parser behavior vs the replan. I verified directly against source.\n- cheapest discriminating test: crosslink swarm init --doc .design/epic-423-swarm-replan.md in a scratch worktree → inspect parsed requirement_groups.len() (expect 0) and agents.len() (expect 1). Or unit-test parse_design_doc(replan_text).requirement_groups.is_empty().\n- severity-if-wrong: the consumed_by target initializes a meaningless single-agent plan; the 26-unit gated swarm never launches. MUST FIX before launch.\n- DIVERGENCE FROM hy3: hy3 wrote 'ZERO work units → swarm launches nothing.' Precise correction: it launches ONE degenerate agent (title fallback at init.rs:184-196), not zero. Launch-blocking substance unchanged.\n\nFINDING F2 [HIGH] The two worktree docs DISAGREE on the four DIS acceptance instances; replan still lists a self-healed instance.\n- statement: replan D0a lists four instances {opencode-fork.md missing; playbook section citations (#429); permissions.md staleness; stale git claim}. plan REQ-DIS1 lists four DIFFERENT instances {opencode-fork.md missing; permissions.md staleness; stale git claim; parser-grammar H2/H3}. The replan's #2 (playbook citations) is SELF-HEALED: agent-orchestration-playbook.md has sections 5.1-5.9 (lines 161-465), contradicting 'unverifiable playbook section citations.' The plan correctly dropped it and added the parser-grammar instance. So the replan (the consumed_by target) carries a stale instance list.\n- why-unverified: replan predates #429's provenance correction + the plan's correction.\n- cheapest discriminating test: diff the two docs' instance lists; confirm playbook 5.1-5.9 exist (they do).\n- severity-if-wrong: DIS acceptance gate trains/tests on a phantom instance (#2 in replan); gate validity undermined. MEDIUM-HIGH.","created_at":"2026-08-24T00:08:27.178437522Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:VGwMZmRn+VH/h+u9cCpYEUAHZKYqStEYNmWI2937cOM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVb2u6mHEDn2APO2Gb7FwfAR0xP/tXB4RKhjHKSfMSXcAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA6jN/pGVhNcyWN4qUNwIIIROVskwuoGztBF6/CRRaTGpfDgWaWgmnGKbBO9JsuMbpRb3iszxPD5PtInmI2s0MDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:VGwMZmRn+VH/h+u9cCpYEUAHZKYqStEYNmWI2937cOM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVb2u6mHEDn2APO2Gb7FwfAR0xP/tXB4RKhjHKSfMSXcAAAAPY3Jvc3Nsa