{"agent_id":"pp3g-d818-independent-second-review-on-433-a-prior-hy3-pass-on","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T00:09:05.790874123Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"c5839371-58e2-4318-bd91-59b479029c0e","author":"pp3g-d818-independent-second-review-on-433-a-prior-hy3-pass-on","content":"INDEPENDENT SECOND REVIEW #433 (Zen-variant) — FINDINGS PART 2/3 (F3, F4, F5).\n\nFINDING F3 [HIGH] DIS instance #3 ('stale git claim in auditor kickoff text') is a phantom; unlocatable in reviewer scope.\n- statement: both worktree docs list 'stale git claim in auditor kickoff text' as a known-broken instance. I grepped the worktree: 'stale git' appears ONLY in the two design docs (plus an unrelated opencode test about git worktree registration). auditor.md, kickoff-custom-template.md, and .crosslink/.claude trees contain no such string. The asserted source is not present.\n- why-unverified: instance source not accessible/identifiable; may live in built-in KICKOFF.md inside the crosslink binary (not inspectable) or operator private notes.\n- cheapest discriminating test: grep -r 'stale git' across ~/.crosslink/rules/kickoff.md, auditor.md, kickoff-custom-template.md, and the crosslink binary's built-in template; confirm presence + staleness. Until located, DIS cannot validate against this instance.\n- severity-if-wrong: if phantom (like playbook citations), the DIS 'must catch all four' criterion is unsatisfiable for that instance. MEDIUM-HIGH. (Confirms hy3 finding C.)\n\nFINDING F4 [MEDIUM] DIS instance #1 (opencode-fork.md missing) has a naming ambiguity: crosslink-fork.md exists.\n- statement: instance #1 asserts 'missing .crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md cited by opencode wrapper.' The file opencode-fork.md is indeed absent (only crosslink-fork.md, agent-orchestration-playbook.md, kickoff-custom-template.md, model-discipline.md exist). BUT a similarly-named, substantive crosslink-fork.md IS present and describes the fork. #427's independent cross-check (D2) confirmed opencode-fork.md ABSENT and that fork knowledge is scattered across docs/research/*.md + the wrapper. So the missing-file premise holds, but (a) the 'cited by opencode wrapper' provenance is unverified from the worktree (no wrapper citation found), and (b) the naming (opencode-fork.md vs crosslink-fork.md) creates risk the DIS graph flags a false positive/negative or the instance is stale/misnamed.\n- why-unverified: cannot locate the wrapper citation of opencode-fork.md in the worktree; naming overlap with crosslink-fork.md unexamined.\n- cheapest discriminating test: locate the wrapper's citation of opencode-fork.md (grep ~/.local/bin/opencode and scripts/); confirm whether the intended target was renamed to crosslink-fork.md (in which case the instance is stale/misnamed).\n- severity-if-wrong: DIS graph may flag the wrong file or miss the real breakage; acceptance-test premise ambiguous. MEDIUM. (NEW vs hy3 — hy3 treated instance #1 as a solid verified instance without the naming caveat.)\n\nFINDING F5 [MEDIUM] Budget-window 'hard limit / terminated' (playbook 5.2) is unimplemented; replan's 'guide' is actually accurate.\n- statement: playbook 5.2 (lines 189-190): 'Budget windows are hard limits. Agents exceeding the budget are terminated.' Source crosslink/src/commands/swarm/budget.rs implements ONLY config/estimate/recommendation + a launch-time gate (launch_budget_aware, lines 222-275): on Block it bail!s (overridable via non-budget-aware launch); on Split it warns-and-launches anyway; there is NO runtime termination of agents. So 'agents exceeding the budget are terminated' is false in source. The replan's 'Budget window: 6h total guide' is MORE accurate than the playbook's 'hard limit.'\n- why-unverified: playbook asserts enforcement; source shows only launch-time block/split (no termination). Whether termination exists in orchestrator/sentinel path is unverified (not in budget.rs; not inspected).\n- cheapest discriminating test: grep -rn 'terminate|kill' crosslink/src/commands/swarm/ (done → none) and check orchestrator/sentinel for any budget_window_s hard cutoff. If absent, the 'hard limit' is aspirational.\n- severity-if-wrong: if not a hard limit, agents can exceed budget and run unbounded (only launch is gated). Reliance on the playbook claim for sequencing is unsound. MEDIUM. DIVERGENCE FROM hy3: hy3 framed this as 'resolve the contradiction in the design doc'; my read is the DESIGN DOC is correct ('guide') and the PLAYBOOK overclaims. Severity lower than hy3's medium-high.","created_at":"2026-08-24T00:09:05.783472536Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:VGwMZmRn+VH/h+u9cCpYEUAHZKYqStEYNmWI2937cOM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVb2u6mHEDn2APO2Gb7FwfAR0xP/tXB4RKhjHKSfMSXcAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAcIyhbe6YzmTHb4Uosn6Rwh83f4WvfstUFR6eUpqmxEVC+koDdCeT+XCTjjWo1LdKAvImVjzTr/hVNVyRiCiNDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:VGwMZmRn+VH/h+u9cCpYEUAHZKYqStEYNmWI2937cOM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVb2u6mHEDn2APO2Gb7FwfAR0xP/tXB4RKhjHKSfMSXcAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJZiFexL0g48gUDj4U9YYFak/dg8QfpQSR/i4ECYQ6qhN8ctdgIJFcZKb0i5aBxgoRZvG6uD7NYHmKhSgZbptQk="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-d818-independent-second-review-on-433-a-prior-hy3-pass-on","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T00:09:41.076550293Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"2893bec9-4842-4040-90bc-088719082abb","author":"pp3g-d818-independent-second-review-on-433-a-prior-hy3-pass-on","content":"INDEPENDENT SECOND REVIEW #433 (Zen-variant) — FINDINGS PART 3/3 (F6, F7, F8, F9).\n\nFINDING F6 [MEDIUM] D1-D9 delta claims inherited single-source from #427 without propagating its explicit uncertainty.\n- statement: replan/plan present D1-D9 (fork deltas) as the foundation for R2 parity probes (P0a-P0d) and R3 verdict (REQ-V1). #427 is explicitly a read-only breadth-first probe with 5 WHAT-NOT-TESTED items (§5) and self-rates D1-D3 v2 status as UNKNOWN-NEEDS-PROBE, D3 v2 as Guess. The design docs do NOT carry forward this uncertainty; they present the deltas as established ('behavioral probes from #427 matrix'). The plan's P0 series IS the re-verification (good) but is gated on R2 (late); early phases (DIS, R0, R1) assume the fork/deltas are real without independent check.\n- why-unverified: #427 self-admits it did NOT run the 16-row hang matrix, did NOT probe opencode2 beta, did NOT fetch upstream llm.ts/provider.ts HEAD.\n- cheapest discriminating test: promote at least one independent fork-vs-source delta confirmation (run the 16-row hang matrix from #427) BEFORE R3 gating, not after; and propagate #427's WHAT-NOT-TESTED into the design docs so R3 isn't treated as confirmed.\n- severity-if-wrong: if any D1-D9 is mischaracterized for v2 (e.g. D2/D3 already landed upstream), the R3 verdict gate could be wrong. MEDIUM. COMPOUNDING: if F1 (parser breakage) stands, R2 probes are never created as work units, so D1-D9 are never re-verified and R3 is unsound by cascade. (NEW insight vs hy3: the parser defect breaks the re-verification path itself.)\n\nFINDING F7 [MEDIUM] Track M assumes projects/server/migration-handoff-summary.md runbook exists; not present in reachable scope.\n- statement: replan Track M: 'Path updates handled systematically by projects/server/migration-handoff-summary.md runbook.' No projects/ directory and no migration-handoff-summary.md exists in this worktree/repo. The runbook is outside the swarm's reachable scope (likely a different projects tree). M1 gated on R1, M4 on R0d — both rest on a runbook whose existence/currency is unverified here.\n- why-unverified: not read; existence/claims unconfirmed from reviewer scope.\n- cheapest discriminating test: locate projects/server/migration-handoff-summary.md, confirm it exists, and verify its cutover/parallel-environment claims are current (not themselves stale like permissions.md).\n- severity-if-wrong: if the runbook is missing or stale, Track M gating rests on a phantom; M-track agents would block or operate on absent instructions. MEDIUM. (Confirms hy3 finding G.)\n\nFINDING F8 [LOW] S1/S2/S3 surface taxonomy omits the user-level plugin/config layer and doesn't flag S1 beta-breaking status.\n- statement: S1/S2/S3 classify the three binaries (opencode2 beta / pp3g fork CLI / crosslink-fork CLI). But #427 D9 shows active controls live in user-level plugin ~/.config/opencode/plugins/plugin.ts (grok blacklist) + ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json (chunkTimeout hygiene), which run tonight and survive fork-binary swap — they are NOT classified under S1/S2/S3. R1a classifies tools x {S1,S2,S3}; tools/config in the user-level layer would be misclassified or missed. Also S1 is defined as 'opencode2 beta' without noting #427's finding that the beta is breaking (plugin API broken, provider schema redesigned), which affects R2 P1-P7 probe feasibility.\n- severity: LOW (plan includes the probes; gap is classification completeness + probe-feasibility note). Note for dispatcher. (Extends hy3 finding H with the user-level-plugin gap.)\n\nFINDING F9 [LIMITATION, not a design defect] Installed binary vs source-tree divergence not fully verifiable from reviewer scope.\n- statement: mandate asked to check divergence between installed /home/claude-code/.cargo/bin/crosslink and source /home/claude-code/projects/crosslink. I verified the SOURCE tree's parser grammar (design_doc.rs) and budget module directly. But I could NOT (a) run 'crosslink swarm init --doc' / 'crosslink --version' (not in reviewer allowlist), nor (b) retrieve git log (git is aliased to rtk git, which is denied in this scope). So the installed binary's actual grammar/version is unverified, and git-log drift between binary era and source is unverified.\n- implication: the parser-grammar finding (F1) should be re-confirmed against the INSTALLED crosslink binary before launch, since the binary may predate the source tree's '## Requirements' requirement.\n- this is a reviewer-scope limitation to report, not a defect in the design docs. (Same class as hy3 finding I; additionally git-log is blocked by the rtk alias here.)","created_at":"2026-08-24T00:09:41.069757040Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:VGwMZmRn+VH/h+u9cCpYEUAHZKYqStEYNmWI2937cOM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVb2u6mHEDn2APO2Gb7FwfAR0xP/tXB4RKhjHKSfMSXcAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABARUPcmDDu/YHugwII6AM64Eij1wW4JWH+C7CTYghKN485j3uhoTTOwrnI4jDV9G6GqH6FVOeJY3h7lk9xtzypDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:VGwMZmRn+VH/h+u9cCpYEUAHZKYqStEYNmWI2937cOM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVb2u6mHEDn2APO2Gb7FwfAR0xP/tXB4RKhjHKSfMSXcAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBK6pCYndgoj3N4fm5Oub0UpWSl8Dj2Ol34EMAsliPfKYYOfgGH61/44lBDSt4jHxbTaVtleJbFlKOcHrVKAVwY="}
